{"path":"chrono/c/CLOCKS_PER_SEC","title":"CLOCKS_PER_SEC","titleHtml":"CLOCKS_PER_SEC","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/chrono/c/CLOCKS_PER_SEC","section":"chrono","kind":"page","summary":"Expands to an expression (not necessarily a compile-time constant) of type std::clock_t equal to the number of clock ticks per second, as returned by std::clock().","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/ctime\">&lt;ctime&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"co2\">#define CLOCKS_PER_SEC /* implementation-defined */</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Expands to an expression (not necessarily a compile-time constant) of type <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/c/clock_t\">std::clock_t</a></span> equal to the number of clock ticks per second, as returned by <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/c/clock\">std::clock()</a></span>. \n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>POSIX defines <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9799919799/basedefs/time.h.html\" data-external=\"1\">CLOCKS_PER_SEC</a> as <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"st0\">'000'</span><span class=\"nu8\">000</span></span></code>, regardless of the actual precision of <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/c/clock\">std::clock()</a></span>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;ctime&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;locale&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/c/clock_t\"><span class=\"kw1031\">std::<span class=\"me2\">clock_t</span></span></a> cps<span class=\"br0\">{</span>CLOCKS_PER_SEC<span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1774\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a>.<span class=\"me1\">imbue</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/locale/locale\"><span class=\"kw1910\">std::<span class=\"me2\">locale</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"en_US.utf8\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1774\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> cps <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>1,000,000</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/c/clock\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>clock</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns raw processor clock time since the program is started <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/c/clock_t\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>clock_t</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  process running time <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(typedef)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/c/chrono/CLOCKS_PER_SEC\">C documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>CLOCKS_PER_SEC</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"chrono","title":"Date and time utilities"},{"path":"chrono/c","title":"C Date and time utilities"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"CLOCKS_PER_SEC","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Expands to an expression (not necessarily a compile-time constant) of type std::clock_t equal to the number of clock…"},{"label":"Notes","note":"POSIX defines CLOCKS_PER_SEC as 1'000'000, regardless of the actual precision of std::clock()."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"clock","note":"returns raw processor clock time since the program is started"},{"label":"clock_t","note":"process running time"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":93,"codeBlockCount":2}
